## Summary

Built the production Apple-native **`Distance`** shared surface (P4 · 0085) at parity with the web source `components/data-display/format/Distance.tsx`, committed as `7e045ad33` (8 source files + gate log, 1111 insertions).

**What it does** (faithful to the web source): takes a caller distance in `miles` or `km` (miles-first precedence), normalizes to SI metres, converts to the user's preferred unit, formats with locale-aware grouping + half-away rounding at the resolved precision (`prop → preference → 2`, clamped 0…20), appends the unit label, and surfaces the raw caller value as a `.help` tooltip — rendering the em-dash sentinel `—` when neither input is finite.

**Architecture binding**: `\.tsUnits` env (P1/S8 `useUnits` parity) + `DistanceModel` state-holder, P1/S9 generated tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade (`Distance.strings`), P1/S11 once-only `view.opened` telemetry. Honest parity note (matching the AnimatedNumber/DateGroupedList precedent): the source is a synchronous formatter with no fetch, so only its real branches (value + empty) are reproduced — no fabricated network states.

